# The energy-line/poison-column claim (wave 34 §B item 1, w33 B's own
# screenshot: the energy line clips under the opponent's side column at
# 1280x800). Seat 0 (human) lands in an ordinary, uncontested Main Phase 1
# with THREE counter types already non-zero on the player (`GameState`'s
# `humancounters=KEY=N,KEY=N` — `GameState.java:1127-1134`,
# `applyCountersToGameEntity`, keyed by `CounterEnumType`'s own constant names:
# `POISON`, `ENERGY`, `EXPERIENCE` — `CounterEnumType.java:496-500`), so a
# screenshot of this scenario shows poison, energy AND experience all at once,
# not just one counter type standing in for the claim. Poison is kept under
# the lethal ten (`GameRules`'s poison state-based action) so the match stays
# up long enough to screenshot.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humancounters=POISON=3,ENERGY=7,EXPERIENCE=2
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Island;Island
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
